ece of shaft(?), cut across length from thick branch, sides pared down asymmetrically, off center, but following flattened octagonal shape. Paring of sides irregular. Nail shaft hole, square, roughly 0.3x0.5 at core center of branch. Thickness uneven","3.5 x 3; H. 1.6-1.9","Zych, I.; inking Woźniak, M.; digitizing Puszkarski, M.","","Pinewood (Abies cilicica).","","2011-10-04 23:44:24","shaft(?)","BE09-57/007/033","Zych, I.","BE09-57_007_033_a, d.JPG","accreted deposit on one side, otherwise well preserved","","1","","","","","Zych, I.; wood identification Zieliński, J.","","","","""5137","BE","9","57","7","016","103","pp","0588-Q-027","","2009_02_03","","Long truncated conical shape,doubling the diameter both ways. Cut from length of branch. Top of handle worked concavely, leaving round knob in the center raised only by depth of carving around it (minimally 0.1mm). Mounting end has 3 cm long slot in center, cut to the outside, inside end squared evenly, 0.1 mm wide. Pierced transversely through slot two holes about 1 cm apart, traces in wood each about 1-2 mm thick, but the peg must have been slightly bigger. Width of mounting element could have been 1.0 at the maximum (short end), if it did not stick out.","L. 7.2; W. 2.25-1.25; H. 1.1-0.5","Zych, I.; inking Woźniak, M.; digitizing Puszkarski, M.","","wood","spr","2011-03-07 11:43:40","handle","BE09-57/007/034","Zych, I.","BE09-57_007_034_a, b.jpg","slit lengthwise, half preserved, surface smooth, inside surface uneven and fluffing","","1","","","","","Zych, I.; wood identification Zieliński, J.","","","","""5138","BE","9","57","7","016","103","pp","0589-Q-028","","2009_02_03","","Long panel with grooved line ornament. One section is rectangular, thicker by half, pierced sideways through the width midway. The top part extends beyond this section, cut obliquely to the width of the tenon on one end (0.9 wide, 0.5 thick and max.0.9 long), cut off at an angle. At opposite end the central panel between grooves, which is equal to the tenon, continues unbroken to the second similar section, worked symmetrically; the gap forms a regular semi-hexagonal open space, possibly for receiving a suitable panel fitted sideways. All edges except for the broken end are clean, well cut. Decoration consists of parallel grooves, shallow and gentle, setting off the side edges and emphasizing the central zone. Crosslines, thinner and fainter, are marked across this central zone marking the edge of the thicker section and parallel on the opposite side, set apart approx. 2 cm, which would also be the anticipated width of cross-panels, same as this panel.","L. 10.9, projecting underside 5.3; W. 1.8, narrower parts 0.9 and 0.8; Th. 0.9, projecting underside by 0.45; Th. tenon 0.4; Dia. hole 0.35","Zych, I.; inking Woźniak, M.; digitizing Puszkarski, M.","","wood","spr","2011-03-07 16:44:34","panel(?)","BE09-57/007/035","Zych, I.","BE09-57_007_035_a, b.JPG","overall good condition, ending of panel seems to be broken off and worn away; unclear whether thinned or split in half","","1","","","","","Zych, I.; wood identification Zieliński, J.","","","","""5140","BE","9","999","999","005","113","pp","0584-Q-023","","2009_01_29","modern(?)","Cylindrical peg with articulated cap of bigger diameter, opposite end rounded by four pared planes to a tip at the center; at this end, two holes pierced through body perpendicular to one another, the first about 0.8 cm from tip, the second 0.5 cm further up.","L. 6.8; Dia. head 1.4; shaft 1.0; hole 0.3-0.25","Zych, I.; inking Woźniak, M.; digitizing Puszkarski, M.","","wood","","2011-03-07 18:29:42","peg","BE09-999/035","Zych, I.","BE09-999_035_a.JPG","missing edge at one end, otherwise complete, good condition","","1","","","according to tag, found a day later, but inconsequential","","Zych, I.","","0.5m NE of BE09-57","","""5141","BE","9","57","1","002","89","P","","","2009_01_29","","","","","","wood; głównie cedr Cedrus atlantica ssp.libani, też: tamaryszek Tamar